---
title: Chicken piccata
servings: 4
tags: [italian, chicken, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
source: Chicken Piccata by America's Test Kitchen, https://pbssocal.org/shows/americas-test-kitchen-from-cooks-illustrated/recipe-chicken-piccata
---

Halve the @boneless skinless chicken breasts{4}(6 to 8 oz each, trimmed)
crosswise, then split the thick halves through the middle to get 12 cutlets.
Pound them between #plastic wrap{} to an even 1/2 inch. Toss with
@kosher salt{2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and leave ~{15%minutes}.

Halve one of the @lemons{2} lengthwise. Trim the ends off one half, quarter it
lengthwise and slice it 1/4 inch thick. Juice the other half and the second
lemon; keep 3 tbsp of juice.

Dredge the cutlets one at a time in the @all-purpose flour{3/4%cup}, shake off
the excess, and set them on a #wire rack{} over a #rimmed baking sheet{}.

Heat 2 tbsp of the @vegetable oil{1/4%cup}(plus 1 tsp) in a 12-inch #skillet{}
over medium-high heat until smoking. Add 6 cutlets, turn the heat to medium,
and cook ~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes} a side until golden. Back to the rack.
Repeat with 2 tbsp more oil and the rest.

Add the last 1 tsp of oil and the @shallot{1}(minced) and cook ~{1%minute}.
Add the @garlic{1%clove}(minced) and cook ~{30%seconds}.

Pour in the @chicken broth{1%cup}, the lemon juice and the lemon slices. Bring
to a simmer, scraping up the browned bits.

Return the cutlets and simmer ~{4%minutes}, turning once. Move them to a
platter. If the sauce is thinner than heavy cream, give it another minute.

Off the heat, whisk in the @unsalted butter{3%tbsp}(cut into 6 pieces), then
stir in the @capers{2%tbsp}(drained) and @parsley{1%tbsp}(minced). Season and
spoon over the chicken.
